{
  "_comment": "Scripted dungeon runs (v2). A run starts when the first player enters a copy of `map` and walks `steps` in order: each step waits for its trigger, then acts. Positions are local to the copy (the instance offset is added). Triggers: enter | cleared:<step id> (every creature that step spawned is dead) | area:<z_below> (a player stands deeper than local z) | hp_below:<step id>:<fraction> (a creature that step spawned is alive below that share of its hit points). A step with `optional: true` is a side slot: it is not part of the chain (the run never waits for it) and fires on its own trigger; its creatures count toward the clear like any other. Actions: spawn (creatures, optional boss_key/template; `assist` narrows how far they answer a fight, so a side room is not pulled by the corridor), open / close (gate ids), message (shown to the copy), chest (loot table at a point), complete. A spawn entry has no fixed level: `role` (roles block) and an optional extra `lvl` offset put it above the run's level, and the role picks its party HP scaling and clear share (`forces`). A spawn entry may carry `harp` (local point; Fluffy's lullaby pedestal). Run level: ref = round(group.ref_max_weight x highest + (1 - ref_max_weight) x average party level), clamped to the dungeon's level_min..level_max, plus the difficulty's level_offset; it is fixed when the run opens. Creature stats follow that level (bosses scale their boss_overrides numbers from the override's stat_level), then the difficulty's hp/damage and the party HP scaling. `key`: the item the leader spends to open a difficulty that asks for keys. Wipe: while a step's closed gates hold a living boss and no living player is past its area, the gates open (respawned players walk back; crossing again seals them). hazards: periodic shoves of every player inside a local z band (and x band, when given) while the run is between from_step and until_step. first_clear_title: granted to everyone in the copy when the run completes. par_s: the gold-medal time of a full clear; medals multiply it. The clock starts when the start gate opens and stops when the run completes; deaths add the difficulty's death_penalty_s and spend its party lives. Spider lair extras: a spawn entry's `hatch` {after_s, into: [entries]} breaks it open into those creatures if it still stands then; a step's `cocoon` {mob, hold_s, hp_share} wraps a random player (stunned until the cocoon is broken, the share of their health lost if it is not); a step's `pools` [{at, radius, duration_s, hp_share_s}] are venom pools that hurt every second. `min_difficulty` on a step or a spawn entry keeps it out of runs below that difficulty (extra waves, twins); a spawn entry's `harp_scale` {difficulty: x} slows Fluffy's harp and `marks` {difficulty: [meta]} sets creature marks such as curse_bleed; a pool with `kind` web is a sticky web patch.",
